.TH SDL_zerop 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_zerop \- Clear an object\(aqs memory to zero, using a pointer.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_zerop(x) SDL_memset((x), 0, sizeof(*(x)))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is wrapper over
.BR SDL_memset
that handles calculating the object size, so there\(aqs no chance of copy/paste errors, and the code is cleaner\[char46]
.PP
This requires a pointer to an object, not an object itself, nor an array\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I x
a pointer to the object to clear\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

